                    <item name="Size" type_name="gh_single" type_code="5">9</item>
                    <item name="Text" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">STEP 1  -  How tall is the tower?
Goal: one number: the total height in feet.
Idea: Derive values from sliders: Floors × Floor-to-floor.
Watch for: Don't type the height in by hand: it has to update
   whenever a slider moves.</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="1">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="2">
                        <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
                          <X>1102.5186</X>
                          <Y>60</Y>
                          <W>252.45947</W>
                          <H>58.0542</H>
